  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps a 5% endpoint but adds a 60-month transition with no sales stop even above 5%, which is the main weakening and favours Northwind's 6.2% flagship. S5 sets a mandatory 8/100k recall with no transition and no sales ban, which burdens Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9/100k, while S4 delays built-in suppression to 36 months for new units, which benefits Halcyon's cost position. S4's 'regulator-approved equivalent' is coded as validated_equivalent_allowed, and S1 scope is read as confirmed incidents, a judgement call the rules treat as acceptable rather than safe."
 },
